    <note id="byG">
      <content>
        <p>There is one world, but it presents two surfaces. To an observer or a forecaster it is an object to watch, simulate, and place predictions on. To a player, that same world is a game to enter and alter. Both sit on the identical checkable, living core, so a player&apos;s action and a forecaster&apos;s prediction are about the same evolving reality. This is why the product is not a game and not a forecasting tool: it is a world that supports both. The architecture also degrades gracefully: if the 3D or video layer fails, the 2D game stays playable, and the world itself keeps running. One world, two ways in, no single point of failure.</p>
      </content>
    </note>
